-- title:
--   Local structure of an end: widehat𝒪≅ W₁[[U,V]]/(UV-(σ₁varpi)^m)
-- statement:
--   Arithmetic data. A prime $q\ge 5$, a nonzero natural number $M'$ with $q\nmid M'$, a prime $\ell\ge 3$ with $\ell\ne q$ and $\ell\nmid M'$; a field $L$ of characteristic zero and $\xi\in L$ a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity, subject to `hι`: there is a ring homomorphism $\iota:L\to\mathbb C$ with $\iota\xi=\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$. Next, $K$ is an intermediate field of $L\subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ and `hK` identifies it with [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) of the $q$-expansion function field [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH (q*ℓ) M')`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79), i.e. the $L$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise image of the rational function field of level $\Gamma_H$ with $N_0=(q\ell)^2M'$ and $H=\ker\bigl((\mathbb Z/N_0)^\times\to(\mathbb Z/(q\ell))^\times\bigr)$.
--
--   Coefficient ring and chart. $A$ is a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$, Henselian local, with algebraically closed residue field, such that $q\in\mathfrak m_A$ (`hAq`) and $\xi$ lies in the image of $A$ (`hξA`); $K$ is an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$. The element $j\in K$, nonzero, has Laurent series the coefficientwise image [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of the $q$-expansion of the modular $j$-function (`hj`). Further, $\varpi$ generates $\mathfrak m_A$ (`hϖ`), and $\varpi_t\in A$ is a tame parameter: $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1}=q\cdot u$ for some unit $u$ (`hϖt`). Throughout, `chartAlgFin A K j` denotes the $A$-subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$, and `jChartFin` the element $j$ of it. The ideal $y$ of this chart algebra is maximal (`hy`), contains $\varpi$ (`hϖy`), and is supersingular in the sense of `hss`: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from the chart algebra to $\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), the set of those $j$-invariants for which every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with that invariant has no nonzero $q$-torsion point.
--
--   The rigidity hypothesis `hArig`. For every point $z$ of the two-chart integral model $X=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) (the pushout glueing $\mathrm{Spec}$ of the $j$-chart and of the $j^{-1}$-chart), for the germ $\varpi_z$ at $z$ of $\varpi$ pulled back along the structure morphism `toBase` to $\mathrm{Spec}\,A$ (`hϖz`), assumed to lie in the maximal ideal of the stalk $\mathcal O_{X,z}$ (`hz`), and for every point $y'$ of `XFin = Spec (chartAlgFin A K j)` with `ιFin`-image $z$ (`hy'`) satisfying the same supersingularity condition at $y'$ (`hss'`), there exist a complete discrete valuation domain $W$, a ring homomorphism $\sigma:A\to W$ with $\mathfrak m_W=(\sigma\varpi)$, power series $f,u,v\in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u,v$ units and $f\equiv X_0X_1^q-X_0^qX_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$ (the congruence to [`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.drinfeldForm q W`](def/DrinfeldCurve_LocalChart.html#L18)), and a ring isomorphism $e$ from the adic completion of $\mathcal O_{X,z}$ at its maximal ideal onto $S=W[[X_0,X_1]]/\bigl(C(\sigma(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))v-fu\bigr)$, such that, writing `toC` for the completion map, `mkS` for the quotient map onto $S$ and `germY` for the homomorphism from the chart algebra to $\mathcal O_{X,z}$ obtained from `ΓSpecIso`, the `ιFin`-comparison isomorphism and the germ at $z$ on the image of `ιFin`, the following seven clauses hold: (1) $e$ carries the image of $a\in A$ to the class of $C(\sigma a)$; (2) for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and every $\tau\in\mathrm{Aut}(K/L)$ with [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L (q*ℓ) ξ (q*ℓ) ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (levelH (q*ℓ) M') γ⁻¹ K τ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29) — the predicate saying that on every quotient $f/g$ of modular forms of weight $k$ for $\Gamma_H(N_0)$ with integral $q$-expansions, $\tau$ realises, after any complex embedding normalised by $\xi\mapsto e^{2\pi i/(q\ell)}$, the substitution by the matrix `conjElemN (q*ℓ) γ⁻¹` — the automorphism $\tau$ maps the chart algebra into itself; (3) for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')\cap\Gamma(\ell)$ and such a $\tau$ preserving the chart algebra, the induced endomorphism is the identity modulo $y'$; (4) for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and such a $\tau$ preserving the chart algebra and inducing the identity modulo $y'$, there are a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, an element $c\in W$ and a matrix $M\in M_2(W)$ with: $\theta$ intertwining $e\circ\mathrm{toC}\circ\mathrm{germY}$ with the action of $\tau$; $\theta$ fixing every constant $C(w)$; $\theta(X_j)\equiv\sum_i M_{ij}X_i$ modulo the square of the ideal generated by the classes of $X_0,X_1$; $c^{q+1}\equiv 1$, $M_{ij}\equiv c\,\gamma_{ij}$ modulo $\mathfrak m_W$; $c\equiv 1$ if $\gamma\in\Gamma(\ell)$; and $c\not\equiv 1$ if $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\tau$ is not the identity on $K$; (5) for integers $a_1,b_1,a_2,b_2$ and primes $P_1,P_2$ of $S$, each not containing both classes of $X_0$ and $X_1$, each containing the class of $C(\sigma\varpi)$ and each containing an element of the shape $a_iX_0+b_iX_1+h$ with $h\in(X_0,X_1)^2$, if $q\nmid a_1b_2-a_2b_1$ then the contractions of $P_1,P_2$ along $e\circ\mathrm{toC}$ are distinct; (6) for a prime $P$ of $S$ as above containing an element $X_0+h$ with $h\in(X_0,X_1)^2$, an element $a$ of the chart algebra has $\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germY}\,a)$ in the contraction of $P$ along $e$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $a$ lies in the image of $\mathfrak m_A$; (7) the series [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L (q*ℓ)`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) (the $q$-expansion of $j$ with exponents multiplied by $q\ell$) lies in $K$ and in the chart algebra, and there are $a_0\in A$ with the difference in $y'$, an integer $e_0\ge 1$ and $h\in(X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ such that $\sum_{i=0}^{e_0}\mathrm{coeff}_{(i,e_0-i)}(h)\,a^ib^{e_0-i}$ is a unit for all $a,b\in W$ not both in $\mathfrak m_W$ with $a^qb-ab^q\in\mathfrak m_W$, and $e$ carries the image of that difference to $\mathrm{mkS}(h)$.
--
--   The opened witness. Data $z,\varpi_z,y'$ as above (hypotheses `hϖz`, `hz`, `hy'`, `hss'`) together with `hy'y`: $y'$ corresponds to the ideal $y$. A complete discrete valuation domain $W_1$, a homomorphism $\sigma_1:A\to W_1$ with $\mathfrak m_{W_1}=(\sigma_1\varpi)$ (`hσ₁`), series $f_1,u_1,v_1$ with $u_1,v_1$ units (`hu₁`, `hv₁`) and $f_1$ congruent to the Drinfeld form modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$ (`hf₁`), and an isomorphism $e_1$ of the completed stalk with $S=W_1[[X_0,X_1]]/\bigl(C(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))v_1-f_1u_1\bigr)$, are given; the hypothesis `hW₁` asserts for this data exactly the seven clauses (1)–(7) listed above.
--
--   Centre, blow-up algebra and Drinfeld reduction. The ideal $J$ of the chart algebra is, by `hJ`, the infimum of all ideals of the form $\tau^{-1}$-contraction of the contraction along $e_1\circ\mathrm{toC}\circ\mathrm{germY}$ of the ideal generated by the classes of $C(\sigma_1\varpi_t)$, $X_0$ and $X_1$, the infimum being taken over $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and chart-preserving $\tau$ with `IsLevelAutAt … γ⁻¹ K τ`. The $A$-subalgebra $B$ of $K$ is, by `hB`, generated over the chart algebra by $\{x\in K:\ x\varpi_t\in J\}$. A valuation subring $W$ of $K$ contains $B$ (`hBW`). The hypothesis `hR1` states that the chart algebra is contained in $B$ and that every element of $K$ is a quotient of two elements of $B$ with nonzero denominator; `hR2` states that $A\to B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation and that $B/(\varpi)$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; `hR3` (five clauses) states that an element of $L$ lies in $W$ exactly when it comes from $A$, that $\mathfrak m_W$ is generated by $\varpi$, that $W$ is a discrete valuation ring, that an element of the chart algebra lies in $y$ exactly when it lies in $\mathfrak m_W$, and that $W$ is the localisation of $B$ at the elements outside $\mathfrak m_W$. The hypothesis `hEQ` (five clauses, summarised here) provides: for every $\mathrm{GF}(q^2)$-algebra structure on the residue field of $A$, a surjection $\rho$ from $B$ onto the Drinfeld coordinate ring [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q (ResidueField A)`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) with kernel the elements of $B$ in $\mathfrak m_W$, compatible with $A\to\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$, and equivariant for the level automorphisms through an element $c$ with $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma,c)\in$ [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) acting by `hAction`, with $c\ne 1$ when $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\tau\ne\mathrm{id}$; stability of $B$ under the level automorphisms for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$; for every prime of $B$ containing $\varpi$, a level automorphism carrying the elements of $B\cap\mathfrak m_W$ into it; divisibility by $\varpi$ of any $b\in B$ all of whose level translates lie in $\mathfrak m_W$; and stability of $W$ under any level automorphism preserving $y$. Finally `hjK`, `hjC` record that [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L (q*ℓ)`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) lies in $K$ and in the chart algebra; $m\ge 1$ satisfies $\varpi^m=\varpi_t\cdot(\text{unit})$ (`hm1`, `hmt`).
--
--   The end. $O$ is a subring of $K$ and `hO` pins it down: there is an element $a$ of the chart algebra lying in $J$, nonzero in $K$, such that, with $B_a$ the $A$-subalgebra generated over the chart algebra by $\{x\in K:\ xa\in J\}$, there is a maximal ideal $P$ of $B_a$ with $O=\{g/h:\ g,h\in B_a,\ h\notin P\}$, such that every element of $y$ lying in $O$ is a non-unit of $O$, and such that $B$ is not contained in $O$.
--
--   Conclusion. With $\mathrm{STK}=\mathcal O_{X,z}$, $\mathrm{CMP}$ its adic completion at the maximal ideal, $\mathrm{toC}$ the canonical map, $S$, $\mathrm{mkS}$ and $\mathrm{germY}$ as above (formed with $W_1,\sigma_1,f_1,u_1,v_1$), the ring $O$ is local and Noetherian, the chart algebra is contained in $O$, and:
--
--   (a) an element of the chart algebra lies in $\mathfrak m_O$ if and only if it lies in $y$;
--
--   (b) for every $f\in O$ there is $a\in A$ whose image lies in $O$ with $f-a$ a non-unit of $O$.
--
--   Moreover there is a ring homomorphism $\Lambda:S\to\widehat O$, the adic completion of $O$ at $\mathfrak m_O$, such that
--
--   (c) $\Lambda(e_1(\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germY}\,c)))$ is the image of $c$ in $\widehat O$ for every $c$ in the chart algebra; and
--
--   (d) for every $N$, $\Lambda$ maps the $N$-th power of the ideal of $S$ generated by the classes of $C(\sigma_1\varpi)$, $X_0$, $X_1$ into the $N$-th power of the ideal of $\widehat O$ generated by the image of $\mathfrak m_O$.
--
--   There is further a ring isomorphism
--   $$\iota_1:\widehat O\;\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }\;\mathrm{UVCrossingModel}\,W_1\,((\sigma_1\varpi)^m)=W_1[[X_0,X_1]]/\bigl(X_0X_1-C((\sigma_1\varpi)^m)\bigr)$$
--   such that
--
--   (e) $\iota_1(\Lambda(\mathrm{mkS}(C(w))))=\mathrm{const}\,w$ for every $w\in W_1$;
--
--   (f) $\iota_1$ sends the image in $\widehat O$ of any $a\in A$ whose image lies in $O$ to $\mathrm{const}(\sigma_1a)$;
--
--   (g) $\sigma_1$ is residually surjective: for every $w\in W_1$ there is $a\in A$ with $w-\sigma_1a\in\mathfrak m_{W_1}$.
--
--   In addition:
--
--   (h) there are $p_0,p_1\in W_1$ and $\alpha,\beta$ in the crossing model with $p_0\notin\mathfrak m_{W_1}$ or $p_1\notin\mathfrak m_{W_1}$, with $p_0^qp_1-p_0p_1^q\in\mathfrak m_{W_1}$, with $\alpha-\mathrm{const}\,p_0$ and $\beta-\mathrm{const}\,p_1$ non-units, and with
--   $$\iota_1(\Lambda(\mathrm{mkS}(X_0)))=\mathrm{V}\cdot\alpha,\qquad \iota_1(\Lambda(\mathrm{mkS}(X_1)))=\mathrm{V}\cdot\beta,$$
--   where $\mathrm U$, $\mathrm V$ are the two distinguished coordinates `UVCrossingModel.U`, `UVCrossingModel.V` of the model; and
--
--   (i) there are an element $a$ of the chart algebra lying in $J$ and nonzero in $K$, an element $c\in O$, and units $\gamma_U,\gamma_V$ of the crossing model such that every $i\in J$ equals $a\cdot o$ for some $o\in O$, such that $a\,c=\varpi_t$ in $K$, and such that $\iota_1$ sends the image of $a$ in $\widehat O$ to $\gamma_V\cdot\mathrm V$ and the image of $c$ to $\gamma_U\cdot\mathrm U$.
--
--   This is the local analysis, over the coefficient ring $W_1$ of an opened Drinfeld chart, of an end of the blow-up of the supersingular chart at its pinned centre $J$: the completed local ring at such an end is a crossing (node) ring $W_1[[U,V]]/(UV-(\sigma_1\varpi)^m)$, in which the two Drinfeld-chart coordinates become $V$ times units with residually $\mathbb F_q$-rational ratio, the centre becomes principal with generator corresponding to $\mathrm{unit}\cdot V$, and its cofactor to $\mathrm{unit}\cdot U$. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_primes_exceptional_igusa_trichotomy_of_end_blowupChart_linked`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_primes_exceptional_igusa_trichotomy_of_end_blowupChart_linked) and by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_ringHom_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_uvCrossingModel_tangent_coords_of_end_blowupChart_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_ringHom_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_uvCrossingModel_tangent_coords_of_end_blowupChart_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked) in the construction of the integral model of the modular curve at $q$ and the determination of its reduction at supersingular points.
